<li id="S4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">*</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">The “Normal” group does not indicate complete health, but rather the absence of the six listed ophthalmic and systemic diseases.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Setting</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In OCT-Biomarker alignment stage, each 244<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>244 central-foveal OCT B-scan is contrastively aligned with its corresponding 3D biomarker embedding using InfoNCE loss (<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) and the AdamW optimizer (learning rate = 1e-4, weight decay = 1e-2), for a total of 50 epochs.
As for the Supervised Instruction Finetuning stage, we jointly fine-tune the LLM and its projector module. To reduce computational cost, we adopt the Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) technique. Training is conducted on a single NVIDIA L40S GPU (48 GB VRAM) for 2 epochs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that both stages use the same <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">eid</span>-based split of the UKBiobank dataset to define training and testing sets, ensuring consistency across the two phases.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE II</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comprehensive performance comparison across models. All metrics (except BERT-score and Macro F1) are scaled to 0–100 (higher is better).</span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
